":\"other compressors under a text wrapper: zlib (any level byte), raw deflate, bz2, xz, lzma-alone, under base64/base64url/hex/base32/base85/binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 = gzip inside std padded base64 ('A familiar wrapper. Something compressed inside.'); D19->D20 showed the lane turns ONE knob the next day, so expect the same wrapper with another squeeze, or the same gzip under another wrapper. Build warmups_codecs.decompress_sweep(t): every wrapper decoder (b64 std/url, padded or not; hex any case/spaced; b32; a85/b85; 8-bit binary) -> magic sniff (1f8b gzip, 78 01/5e/9c/da zlib, BZh bz2, fd377a585a xz, 5d0000 lzma-alone) -> decompress; raw deflate by trial zlib.decompress(b,-15) when no magic. Return the first slug-gated text. Register as a free codec for Mastery fragments (36-char per-fragment members). Fixtures: each compressor x each wrapper, + 6-10 char Mastery fragments. Cost cap < 0.05 s per blob.\"},\n {\"id\":\"raw-deflate-gzip-quirks\",\"concept\":\"gzip/deflate stream quirks: headerless deflate, truncated CRC trailer, FNAME/FCOMMENT/FEXTRA header fields, multi-member / concatenated gzip\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Knob on D21's codec. gzip.decompress raises on a missing/short trailer and on trailing garbage; use zlib.decompressobj(31) and loop over unused_data for concatenated members; wbits=-15 for raw deflate, 47 for auto zlib/gzip. Header with FNAME (b64 'H4sICA') carries a filename that may hint the next layer -- surface it in the solver's notes, never as the answer. Fixtures: truncated, FNAME/FCOMMENT set, 2-3 concatenated members, mtime != 0, xfl/OS variants.\"},\n {\"id\":\"decompress-then-redecode\",\"concept\":\"inflated text is another seen codec (gzip of hex/rot13/Morse/b64), or an old free transform over the compressed wrapper (reversed / rot13 / Atbash base64 of gzip)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Stacks a seen family on D21's new one. After every decompress, run decode_chunk + CANDIDATES on the output (depth cap 3, slug gate). Before the b64 magic sniff, also try undoing rev/rot13/Atbash/ROT47 when the text is b64-ish but not valid (rot13 of 'H4sI' = 'U4fV', reversed ends 'Is4H'). Fixtures: gzip(hex(text)), gzip(rot13(text)), rot13(b64(gzip)), rev(b64(gzip)), b64(gzip(b64(text))).\"},\n {\"id\":\"text-armor-wrappers\",\"concept\":\"text armor wrappers around a body: data: URI, PEM -----BEGIN-----, PGP ASCII armor (=CRC24), MIME part / email (Content-Transfer-Encoding), Intel HEX / Motorola S-record, JSON/XML envelope\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'A familiar wrapper' read literally. Build warmups_codecs.unarmor(t): data:[mime][;base64], PEM/PGP (strip headers, verify CRC24 when present), email.message_from_string (decode each part by its CTE), Intel HEX (:LLAAAATT...CC records, checksum) and S-records -> bytes; then the normal pipeline incl. decompress_sweep. Fixtures: each armor over plain text and over gzip.\"},\n {\"id\":\"archive-container-in-base64\",\"concept\":\"an archive as the wrapper: zip / tar / tar.gz / 7z / cpio / ar member inside base64 or hex\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'wrapper'/'package'/'bundle' puns. Cue: b64 'UEsDB' (zip), 'N3q8ryc' (7z), gzip that inflates to 'ustar' at offset 257 (tar), '070701' cpio, '!<arch>' ar. Read every member (stored or deflated; try password b'infected' if encrypted), decode each with the pipeline, join in archive order. zipfile/tarfile stdlib; py7zr in .venv (check solver import allowance). Fixtures per container, 1 and 3 members.\"},\n {\"id\":\"third-party-compressors\",\"concept\":\"non-stdlib compressors: zstd, lz4 frame, brotli, snappy framed, LZO\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Magic: zstd 28b52ffd (b64 'KLUv/'), lz4 frame 04224d18 (b64 'BCJNGA'), snappy framed ff060000734e61507059, brotli has none (trial decode, slug gate). .venv has zstandard, lz4, brotli (+ CLIs in .venv/bin); snappy/LZO need small pure-python decoders. Guard imports (ImportError -> skip) so solvers stay runnable on Homebase. Fixtures under base64 and hex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lzstring-js\",\"concept\":\"LZ-String (JS) compressToBase64 / compressToEncodedURIComponent / compressToUTF16\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A web-familiar compressor with no magic: base64-alphabet text (URI form uses '+' and '$', no '/') that is not b64-of-a-magic; UTF16 form = dense CJK-range chars. Pure-python decompress (~60 lines, port of pieroxy lz-string), slug-gated. Fixtures for all three forms + Mastery fragments.\"},\n {\"id\":\"rle-lzw-text-compression\",\"concept\":\"text-level compression: run-length encoding, LZ77 tuples, LZW code lists, Huffman with an included code table\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Keyless 'pressure'/'squeeze' puns without binary bytes. RLE both orders ('3a2b' / 'a3b2', count>=1, digits escaped?); LZ77 '(o,l,c)' tuples; LZW = integer list whose first values are ASCII codes and later ones >= 256 (initial dict 256, also 8-bit+clear-code variants); Huffman: a '{char: bits}' table + bit string. Crib-gated decoders + fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"middle-endian-pdp\",\"concept\":\"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words: UTF-32 or u32 char codes\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Retry: attempt 1 FAILED the lib lint ('call __import__() not allowed' in lib/warmups_codecs.py) -- use normal imports. Lower priority now that D21 left the byte-order family, but a 'Same bar' callback stays possible. Hex whose 4-byte words read neither as utf-32-le nor -be: 'N' as UTF-32 in PDP order = 00 00 4e 00. Try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM is the cue.\"},\n {\"id\":\"byte-family-mastery-cost\",\"concept\":\"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; restoring the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch solved 103 sets in 0.34 s (so D20's 18.6 s was not inherent). Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, and time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\"},\n {\"id\":\"case-and-digit-loss\",\"concept\":\"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse -> UPPERCASE hex, D17 Bacon -> a-p).\"},\n {\"id\":\"transposition-mastery-joint\",\"concept\":\"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked misses it (a D21 generalize worker's intermediate run left 'Master:i rbsk-...'). Keep the slug-gated per-line rail pass; register any future transposition decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line.\"},\n {\"id\":\"affine-free-strict\",\"concept\":\"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n {\"id\":\"chepy-cyberchef-cue\",\"concept\":\"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode, gzip/zlib/bzip2 decompress, lz_string; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n {\"id\":\"base92\",\"concept\":\"base92\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"chepy from_base92 / CyberChef From Base92 decode it; cue = printable minus double-quote and backtick.\"},\n {\"id\":\"base65536\",\"concept\":\"base65536 / base2048 / base32768\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"chepy from_base65536; others need pip (base2048) - install only if seen.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bifid-adfgvx\",\"concept\":\"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mime-encoded-word\",\"concept\":\"MIME encoded-word headers\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=. Body-level MIME wrappers are in text-armor-wrappers.\"},\n {\"id\":\"esoteric\",\"concept\":\"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"tool\",\"detail\":\"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n {\"id\":\"misc-tables\",\"concept\":\"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n {\"id\":\"homoglyph\",\"concept\":\"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"tool\",\"detail\":\"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"},\n]\na=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nbody=\"## Readiness gaps\\n\\n```json\\n[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n```\\n\"\ns=s[:a]+body\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\nf=reference/coverage/warmups.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{a=NR} /^## Readiness gaps/{print NR-a-1}' $f; python3 -c \"\nimport json,re\nt=open('$f').read(); j=json.loads(t.split('\\`\\`\\`json')[1].split('\\`\\`\\`')[0])\ns=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in j if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('warmups:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('warmups:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(j),'pending',len(pend),pend); print(set(g.keys()) for g in j[:1])\"; wc -l $f","description":"Apply coverage atlas edits and validate JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":100390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94f5f332-5b5b-4cbc-81e1-02da939b09bc","uuid":"7b5f38c7-5646-43b3-b4b7-d2b4f7d703ad","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:23:46.400Z","request_id":"req_011CgFTFrX7HqikFrEoP1dNm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NBf1XpWQDCzuyj9GgTwNd5":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/warmups.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(s.count(a),a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"text as one BIG integer, or a knob on an older day's codec (code-unit escapes byte-swapped, bit order, alphabet).\nSnapshot 2026-10-20 (after D20; every gap from the D19 list is built; the queue below is new).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"text as one BIG integer, or a k